  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\nOriginally a gardening term meaning to prepare the roots of a tree before transplanting ({根|ね} = root, {回|まわ}し = going around). Now used for business and political preparation.\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nA key concept in Japanese business culture. Decisions are often made informally through {根回|ねまわ}し before being formally approved in meetings, which helps maintain {和|わ} (harmony) and avoid public disagreements.\n\nUSAGE:\nCommon in:\n- Business negotiations\n- Political decisions\n- Organizational changes\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {根回|ねまわ}しをする - to do groundwork\n- {根回|ねまわ}しが{必要|ひつよう} - groundwork is necessary\n- {事前|じぜん}の{根回|ねまわ}し - prior preparation",
